      {
        "id": "ac-part-10",
        "title": "Part X: OPEN QUESTIONS",
        "subtitle": "Negation, quantification, proof, computation, the origin of gravity, the boundary of consciousness — questions the system raises.",
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "ac-part-10-intro",
            "title": "Introduction",
            "spine": "Version 3.",
            "status": "revised",
            "children": [],
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p1",
                "text": "Version 3.0 asked: Why does awareness move at all? Version 4.0 answers: because instinct compels it.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "instinct"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p2",
                "text": "But new questions emerge:",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "setup",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p3",
                "text": "Negation: What does ¬ν mean? Is there ¬* where ¬*ν =* ν?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p4",
                "text": "Quantification: Can we count ν or measure τ strength? Is all quantification ≈?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p5",
                "text": "Proof: What does proof mean when axioms are mutually constitutive?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p6",
                "text": "Computation: Is this system computable, or purely descriptive?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p7",
                "text": "The origin of gravity: The causal chain begins with g. But why does g exist? This system takes g as given—the 'unmoved mover.' Is there something beneath gravity?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "gravity"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p8",
                "text": "The boundary of consciousness: κ ≝ θ ∧ endo(θ). But how much endo(θ) is required? Is there a spectrum of consciousness, or is it binary?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "consciousness"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-intro-p9",
                "text": "Artificial consciousness: If κ requires θ requires i requires g, can a system without physical gravity develop consciousness? Or does 'gravity' generalize to any fundamental relational force?",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "consciousness",
                  "gravity"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference",
            "title": "10.1 The Self-Reference",
            "spine": "This document uses the system to describe the system.",
            "status": "revised",
            "children": [],
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p10",
                "text": "This document uses the system to describe the system. The axioms are stated using operators that presuppose the axioms. What you hold now is noemata (ν*) that crossed the Threshold. It becomes σ only if you cognisce it.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "threshold",
                  "noemata"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p11",
                "text": "The bootstrap is not vicious—it is demonstrative. The system enacts its own principles. It emerged through omniperegrination, constellated around an axis, crossed Thresholds through exologue. The meta-story is the content.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "omniperegrination",
                  "exologue",
                  "axis"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p12",
                "text": "And now the causal chain completes the circle: the gravity that binds atoms caused instinct in biological systems. That instinct, combined with memory, produced thought. Thought, combined with awareness, produced life. Consciousness emerged when thought reflected on itself. And consciousness, exercising the five habits, produced this document—which now describes the process that produced it.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": [
                  "consciousness",
                  "instinct",
                  "gravity",
                  "thought",
                  "memory",
                  "life"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p13",
                "text": "─────────────────────────────────────",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p14",
                "text": "It's the questions, not the answers.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p15",
                "text": "Paradoxes resolve through paradoxes.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p16",
                "text": "Each axiom holds because the others hold.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p17",
                "text": "g causes i. i causes ω. ω experiences ν. ν reflects on ν.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p18",
                "text": "ν is the substance. σ is the truth. E is the anchor.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p19",
                "text": "A =* A",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "claim",
                "linkedTerms": []
              },
              {
                "id": "ac-part-10-10-1-the-self-reference-p20",
                "text": "And that is enough.",
                "status": "revised",
                "spineRole": "setup",
                "linkedTerms": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
